<Component>
	<Description>
		Two-input NOR gate.
		The input threshold is the midpoint of the configured supply levels:
		Vth = (vpos + vneg) / 2.
		An input voltage strictly above Vth is interpreted as HIGH; an input at or below Vth is LOW.
		The output is driven to vpos for HIGH and vneg for LOW.
		Enter optional supply levels in the value field, for example: vpos=5.0 vneg=0.0.
		If omitted, vpos defaults to 5.0 V and vneg defaults to 0.0 V.
		These are ideal, zero-delay logic gates with electrical voltage levels, not transistor-level models.
	</Description>
